{%- comment -%}
  "Loved by Women. Noticed by Others." section (copy of the goda.co block): a serif title and one line under it, a row of customer review cards (picture, 5 stars, the review, "Name | Verified Customer" and two small tags), round arrows with dots under the row, a black Add To Cart button and a small "Money Back Guarantee" line with a tick.
  Desktop: 3 cards in a row. Phones (580px and narrower): 1 card at a time, swipe or use the round arrows. The arrows and dots only appear when there are more cards than fit on the screen (like the original: with only 2 cards on desktop you simply see the 2 cards, centred).
  No slider app and no slider library, just the browser's own scrolling, so it loads fast. Pictures load only when they get near the screen.
  WHERE: best as its own full-width section: Online Store > Themes > Customize > Product page > Add section > Custom Liquid, drag it where you want it, paste this in.
  If you paste it inside a narrow column instead, set mb_bleed to false.
  EDIT YOUR CONTENT BELOW. Do not use a straight apostrophe (') in the text, use &#39; instead, and write & as &amp;
  !!! THE TWO REVIEWS AND THE TWO PICTURES BELOW ARE THE ORIGINAL ONES FROM goda.co. THEY ARE ONLY HERE SO YOU CAN SEE THE SECTION WORKING. Do NOT publish another brand's customers and reviews on your own store: replace every card with REAL reviews from YOUR customers (with their permission), and upload your own pictures in Shopify admin > Content > Files, then paste your own links.
  mb_title = the title. mb_sub = the line under it (leave empty to hide it).
  mb_slides = the review cards, separated by @@ , and each card written as   PICTURE LINK ||| THE REVIEW ||| NAME ||| TAG ; TAG
  Example of one card:   https://yourstore.com/file.jpg ||| Love it! ||| Anna K. ||| Self Love ; Confidence    (the tags are separated by a semicolon, leave the last part empty for no tags, add as many cards as you like).
  mb_verified = the word after the name (for example Verified Customer). Leave empty to show only the name.
  mb_btn_text = the button text (leave empty to hide the button). mb_btn_link = where it goes. A link that starts with # (for example #product) smoothly scrolls to that spot on the page, and if there is no such spot it scrolls to the Add to cart form instead.
  mb_guarantee = the line next to the tick under the button (leave empty to hide it).
  mb_ratio = the shape of every card picture as width / height (1 / 1 = square, 4 / 5 = a little taller).
  mb_color_title = title and the line under it. mb_color_text = review text, names, tags and the guarantee line. mb_color_star = the five stars (the original uses this light blue). mb_color_accent = round arrows, dots and tag outlines. mb_color_arrow = the arrow shapes inside the circles. mb_color_check = the little tick next to the name. mb_card_bg / mb_card_border = card colour / its outline. mb_bg = band colour (transparent = none).
  mb_btn_bg / mb_btn_color = button colour / its writing. mb_btn_radius = how round the button is. mb_btn_w / mb_btn_h = button width (on desktop, and the most it gets on phones) / height.
  mb_title_d / mb_title_m = title size on desktop / phone. mb_pad_d / mb_pad_m = space above, left-right and below the content on desktop / phone, written as top left-right bottom, for example 48px 20px 56px.
  mb_bleed = true stretches the band edge to edge across the screen. mb_top / mb_bottom = space above and below the block.
{%- endcomment -%}
